    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1131">

                <pb facs="1110" n="944" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg944"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/21477</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of War </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State, presenting his compliments to the Honorable the Secretary
                    of War, has the honor to enclose a translation of a note in which the Mexican
                    Ambassador requests the release of twenty-seven Mexican soldiers who it is
                    stated, when pursued into Texas by malefactors, were arrested there by the
                    American authorities, and to ask that the Ambassador’s request be complied with
                    if no objection is perceived.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
